  <section class="wrap fiche-body">
    <div>
      <h2>The vibe</h2>
      <p>Perched on the hills above Grimaud, La Baie des Voiles offers a panoramic view over the Gulf of Saint-Tropez. The former "Château Rose" (the establishment is also a hotel) serves hotel-restaurant cuisine in a setting worth the detour, dog or not: grilled fish, composed salads, seafood risotto.</p>

      <h2>What to know before you go</h2>
      <p>The restaurant is explicitly listed on the "dog-friendly restaurants" page published by the Grimaud tourist office (grimaud-provence.com/preparez/restaurants-dog-friendly-grimaud/) — a top-tier official source. No specific rule (terrace only, dog size) is published elsewhere: it's best to ask when you arrive. On the quality side, the Tripadvisor rating of 4.2/5 is still based on a limited number of reviews (5 recorded), to take as an indication rather than a definitive verdict.</p>
      <div class="callout">Coco's tip: book ahead, especially in season — the view draws crowds and the best tables go fast.</div>

      <h2>Nearby</h2>
      <p>The village of Grimaud and its medieval castle are a few minutes away by car.</p>
